---
/*
  The landing is its own surface, not the docs index wearing a headline. It
  answers, in order: what this is, what is inside, what a page actually looks
  like, how to use it and who it is for — and then says what is still missing
  instead of letting the reader discover the gap on their own.

  Every number and every sample below is real content from this repository, and
  the closing disclosure names exactly the topics this Atlas does not cover yet.
*/
import { modules, pages, getLocalizedPath } from '../data/curriculum.mjs';
import { t } from '../data/ui-text.mjs';

interface Props { locale: 'es' | 'en' }

const { locale } = Astro.props;
const copy = t(locale);
const en = locale === 'en';
const base = en ? '/en/' : '/';
const practiceCount = pages.filter((page) => page.kind === 'practice').length;

const words = en
  ? {
      display: ['Learn DevOps', 'by reading how it', 'actually behaves.'],
      lede: 'A DevOps reference for developers who already code: concepts explained to build a mental model, tools documented as they behave, and walkthroughs that carry one application from your machine to an automated deployment.',
      whatIs: 'What DevOps is',
      start: 'Start with Foundations',
      browse: 'Browse tools A–Z',
      whatInside: 'What is inside',
      insideLede: 'Eight modules that follow the path of a change: read the machine, collaborate on the code, put it on a server, package it, test it on every change, take it to production, hold it up as it grows, and describe that machine in a file. Read them in order, or go straight to the one you need.',
      sample: 'What a page looks like',
      sampleLede: 'Pages separate the boundaries a request crosses, then show the evidence that tells them apart — real commands, real output.',
      sampleCaption: 'From Foundations · investigate a local application',
      howTo: 'How to use it',
      use: [
        {
          title: 'In order, or by lookup',
          body: 'Modules run 01 to 08 and each leans on the previous one. You can also come in through search or the A–Z index: every page states which module it belongs to and what is worth knowing first.',
        },
        {
          title: 'For people who already code',
          body: 'It assumes you can write code, use an editor, and read an error. It does not teach programming from zero: it starts at the point where that code has to run somewhere.',
        },
        {
          title: 'In Spanish and English',
          body: 'Every page exists in full in both languages, not as a half-finished translation. Switch language whenever you like and carry on where you were.',
        },
      ],
      missing: 'Right now the Atlas runs from reading a machine to shipping a version, watching it, rolling it back, and describing the infrastructure in a file. What you will not find here yet: public clouds, Kubernetes in depth, or security.',
      openSource: 'Free, no sign-up.',
      backToTop: 'Back to top',
    }
  : {
      display: ['Aprende DevOps', 'leyendo cómo se', 'comporta de verdad.'],
      lede: 'Referencia de DevOps para quien ya programa: conceptos explicados para construir un modelo mental, herramientas documentadas como se comportan y prácticas que llevan una misma aplicación de tu máquina a un despliegue automático.',
      whatIs: 'Qué es DevOps',
      start: 'Empezar por Fundamentos',
      browse: 'Ver herramientas A–Z',
      whatInside: 'Qué hay dentro',
      insideLede: 'Ocho módulos que siguen el recorrido de un cambio: leer la máquina, colaborar sobre el código, ponerlo en un servidor, empaquetarlo, probarlo en cada cambio, llevarlo a producción, sostenerlo cuando crece y describir esa máquina en un archivo. Puedes leerlos en orden o entrar directo al que necesites.',
      sample: 'Cómo se ve una página',
      sampleLede: 'Las páginas separan las fronteras que atraviesa una petición y muestran la evidencia que las distingue: comandos reales, salida real.',
      sampleCaption: 'De Fundamentos · investigar una aplicación local',
      howTo: 'Cómo usarlo',
      use: [
        {
          title: 'En orden o suelto',
          body: 'Los módulos van del 01 al 08 y cada uno se apoya en el anterior. También puedes entrar por el buscador o por el índice A–Z: cada página dice a qué módulo pertenece y qué conviene saber antes.',
        },
        {
          title: 'Para quien ya programa',
          body: 'Asume que sabes escribir código, usar un editor y leer un error. No enseña a programar desde cero: empieza en el punto donde ese código tiene que correr en alguna parte.',
        },
        {
          title: 'En español y en inglés',
          body: 'Cada página existe completa en los dos idiomas, no como traducción a medias. Cambias de idioma cuando quieras y sigues donde estabas.',
        },
      ],
      missing: 'Por ahora el Atlas llega desde leer una máquina hasta desplegar una versión, observarla, revertirla y describir la infraestructura en un archivo. Todavía no encontrarás aquí nubes públicas, Kubernetes a fondo ni seguridad.',
      openSource: 'Gratis y sin registro.',
      backToTop: 'Volver arriba',
    };
---

<div class="landing">
  <section class="landing__hero">
    <h1 class="landing__display">
      {words.display.map((line) => <span>{line}</span>)}
    </h1>
    <p class="landing__lede">{words.lede}</p>
    <p class="landing__actions">
      <a class="landing__cta" href={`${base}what-is-devops/`}>{words.whatIs}</a>
      <a class="landing__ghost" href={getLocalizedPath('foundations.overview', locale)}>{words.start}</a>
      <a class="landing__ghost" href={`${base}tools/`}>{words.browse}</a>
    </p>
    <dl class="landing__facts">
      <div><dt>{modules.length}</dt><dd>{copy.modules.toLowerCase()}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>{pages.length}</dt><dd>{copy.pages}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>{practiceCount}</dt><dd>{copy.practices}</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="landing__section">
    <h2>{words.whatInside}</h2>
    <p class="landing__intro">{words.insideLede}</p>
    <div class="landing__grid">
      {modules.map((module) => (
        <a class="mcard" href={getLocalizedPath(`${module.id}.overview`, locale)}>
          <span class="mcard__no">{String(module.order).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
          <h3>{module.label[locale]}</h3>
          <p>{module.summary[locale]}</p>
          <ul class="mcard__pages">
            {module.pages.map((page) => <li>{page.label[locale]}</li>)}
          </ul>
          <ul class="mcard__tools">
            {module.tools.map((tool) => <li>{tool}</li>)}
          </ul>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="landing__section landing__sample">
    <div>
      <h2>{words.sample}</h2>
      <p class="landing__sample-lede">{words.sampleLede}</p>
      <p class="landing__sample-caption">{words.sampleCaption}</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="term">
      <figcaption class="term__bar">
        <span class="term__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>bash</span>
      </figcaption>
      <pre><code><span class="term__p">$</span> ss -lnt | grep ':8080'
<span class="term__o">LISTEN 0  511  127.0.0.1:8080  0.0.0.0:*</span>
<span class="term__p">$</span> curl -i http://127.0.0.1:8080/health
<span class="term__ok">HTTP/1.1 200 OK</span>
<span class="term__o">{'{"status":"ok"}'}</span>

<span class="term__p">$</span> curl -i http://127.0.0.1:9090/health
<span class="term__err">curl: (7) Failed to connect to 127.0.0.1 port 9090: Connection refused</span></code></pre>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="landing__section">
    <h2>{words.howTo}</h2>
    <ul class="landing__use">
      {words.use.map((item) => (
        <li>
          <h3>{item.title}</h3>
          <p>{item.body}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <div class="landing__foot">
    <p>{words.missing}</p>
    <p>{words.openSource}</p>
  </div>

  <button type="button" class="landing__totop" aria-label={words.backToTop} data-atlas-top>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="M12 19V5M5 12l7-7 7 7" />
    </svg>
  </button>
</div>

<script>
  /*
    Appears once the hero has scrolled past — before that, the sticky header's
    wordmark already is the way home, so a second one would be noise.
  */
  const button = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-atlas-top]');
  const hero = document.querySelector('.landing__hero');
  if (button && hero) {
    const sync = () => {
      button.toggleAttribute('data-visible', hero.getBoundingClientRect().bottom < 0);
    };
    window.addEventListener('scroll', sync, { passive: true });
    sync();
    button.addEventListener('click', () => window.scrollTo({ top: 0, behavior: 'smooth' }));
  }
</script>
